think r2's Circle consumes signatures at act-time and keeps only points/requests, so the resting state alone cannot re-prove consent after travel. The crux for r3, mirroring fairtrade_cert_bron's still_satisfied: carry the signature that authorized each act, so a recipient re-verifies every act offline.
think Refactored r2 additively — factored the verification half of join_signed/request_signed into public verify_join/verify_request (no circle touched), so a traveled record can re-check consent with no live state. r2 witness re-ran GREEN.
think Built SignedCircle keeping a join sig per member and a request sig per link beside r1's live circle; render to format skate-circle-v1, parse to a PortableCircle owning its buffers; still_consented re-verifies every carried sig, rebuild replays through r2's verified paths into an equal circle whose verdicts match.
obs Byte-for-byte proven by rendering two independently-built identical signed circles (kumara.sign is deterministic with null noise) and comparing bytes; a flipped carried signature refuses BadConsent offline. Unknown field, bad header, missing circle id, bad hex each refuse. GREEN first pass; TAME + width clean first pass.
